<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aghoreshwara Temple</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aghoreshwara Temple is a stone temple to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikkeri">Ikkeri</a> in the Shimoga district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It was built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keladi-nayakas">Keladi Nayakas</a> when Ikkeri was their capital in the 16th century, and combines <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a>, Vijayanagara and other styles. A shrine to Parvati stands beside it.</p></div>
